@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Get ALL Services (Standard Pagination applied automatically)
# Expected: Returns data with a "pagination" object and "total" count
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services

### 2. Search Services by Keyword
# Expected: Finds "Washing Machine Repair" because "washing" matches the regex
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services?search=washing

### 3. Filter Services by Price (Less Than or Equal to $50)
# Notice the syntax: price[lte]=50
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services?price[lte]=50

### 4. Sort Services by Price (Highest First)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services?sort=-basePrice

### 5. Pagination Test: Limit to 1 result per page
# Expected: count is 1, and pagination.next shows page 2 (if you have multiple services)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services?limit=1&page=1

### 6. Select only specific fields
# Expected: Returns ONLY the name and basePrice, stripping out descriptions and arrays
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services?select=name,basePrice

### 7. Get Providers sorted by Rating (Highest First)
# (Assuming Jane got that 5-star review in Phase 15!)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/providers?sort=-rating